    "body": "@shreyateeza if you do `git rebase -i HEAD~N` where N is the number of commits (3 here I suppose) you can edit your commits, including dropping them.  You can then do `git push --force` to push your revised commits to this PR.\r\n\r\nHaving said that, it seems like instead of going for -er, we'd like to go for implementor everywhere, so that would need to change as well.",
